    "Under the RBI Master Direction on Know Your Customer (KYC) / PMLA Rules, determine the \u2018beneficial owner\u2019(s) of Customer Company X given (i) shareholding below the ownership threshold (A 9%, B 9%, Trust T 12%, balance widely held) and (ii) shareholder agreement conferring Company A the right to appoint 3/5 directors and veto key policy decisions. Classify each BO basis as ownership, control (including through arrangements), or the \u2018senior managing official\u2019 fallback, and specify the Customer Due Diligence to be carried out for the customer, BOs, and persons acting on behalf of the customer (authorised signatories/POA).",
    "For a company customer with a trust as one shareholder, apply the RBI KYC Direction\u2019s BO identification requirements for (a) companies and (b) trusts: identify which natural persons must be treated as BOs of Company X (including any natural person behind Company A\u2019s control rights and the trust\u2019s beneficiaries/trustee/settlor/protector, as applicable), and state what KYC/OVD evidence and verification steps are required for each category (customer entity, BOs, and representatives).",
    "Interpret \u2018controlling ownership interest\u2019 and \u2018control\u2019 for BO determination under RBI KYC norms where no shareholder meets the ownership threshold but one minority shareholder (Company A) has board appointment rights and veto/negative control. Identify the natural person(s) to be captured as BOs and when the Regulated Entity must rely on the \u2018senior managing official\u2019 approach; additionally, list the full CDD perimeter (customer, BOs, authorised persons, beneficial owners of the trust shareholder) and the documentary/registry/board-resolution evidence typically relied upon."
